## ⚠️ 3. Common Pitfalls & How to Avoid Them

| Pitfall | Root Cause | Solution |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`Property 'language' does not exist on useTranslation()`** | Context provides `locale` instead of `language` | Standardize interface property names: always check the definition before destructuring. |
| **White-screen crash on missing key** | Accessing nested objects (`dict[section][key]`) when section is undefined | Use flat dot-notation keys (`"settings.workspace.title"`) or safe optional chaining with guaranteed fallback. |
| **`tsc` failure on strict builds** | One dictionary has extra or missing keys | Define an interface `TranslationKeys` or type `Record<string, string>` and enforce exact symmetry. |
| **Dropped dynamic variables in fallback** | Fallback string provided as plain string without token interpolation | Run `replaceAll('{k}', v)` across both dictionary strings AND fallback defaults. |
| **Server vs Client string mismatch** | Backend sends dynamic labels (e.g. task suggestions, API status codes) | Create a mapping function for known backend enums, or localize backend responses at the source. |
| **Unlocalized dynamic tabs or step arrays** | Hardcoding switch/case statements over dynamic config arrays | Use dynamic template keys `t(`workflows.tab.${tab.id}`, tab.label)` preserving runtime extensibility. |
| **Stale top-level module constants on locale switch** | Calling `t()` inside static module-level arrays (`const TABS = [{ label: t(...) }]`) | Define static arrays with `{ key, labelKey, labelFallback }` and call `t(tab.labelKey, tab.labelFallback)` inside the component render loop so UI re-renders on language toggle. |
| **Enum & Status badge mistranslation** | Translating server state enums (`running`, `completed`, `failed`) inline with brittle ternaries | Create dedicated translation maps with fallbacks: `t(`workflows.runs.status_${status}`, status)` to prevent unhandled enum crashes. |
| **Invisible unlocalized strings in UI** | Localizing inner text but forgetting `placeholder`, `aria-label`, and `title` | Always check search inputs, icon buttons, shortcut badges (e.g. `⌘K`), and tooltip texts for direct English strings. |
| **Incomplete foreign language purge** | Removing UI dictionary entries but leaving language detection regex, AI system prompts, starter templates, or API error responses in foreign language | Perform full audit: (1) language detector regex (`[\u0400-\u04FF]` for Cyrillic/Ukrainian), (2) LLM prompt directives & examples, (3) starter project templates/cards, (4) backend API route error strings, (5) `<html lang="...">` and font fallbacks. |
| **Hardcoded date/calendar formatting in utility helpers** | Calling `toLocaleDateString('en-US')` or static weekday lists (`['M', 'T', 'W', ...]`) in logic files outside React components | Parameterize logic helpers with active `locale: 'uk' | 'en'` (defaulting safely to `'en'` or `'uk'`) so calendar days and date formatting match active language without breaking existing unit tests. |
| **Untyped router callbacks in strict TS builds** | Writing `NavLink style={({ isActive }) => ...}` triggers implicit `any` in strict TypeScript setups | Explicitly annotate callback arguments: `({ isActive }: { isActive: boolean }) => ...`. |
| **Unsanitized quotes in env/config token helpers** | Env values loaded with wrapping quotes (e.g. `PROJECT="my-id"`) injected into API URLs | Always sanitize extracted config: `val.trim().replace(/^["']|["']$/g, "")` before building endpoint paths. |
| **React Runtime `NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node'`** | Chrome automatic translation or browser extensions alter DOM (wrapping text in `<font>` or merging sibling text nodes) when foreign strings leak into UI or during step transitions. On unmount/re-render, React reconciler crashes. | 1) Add `<html translate="no" class="notranslate">` and `<meta name="google" content="notranslate" />`. 2) Mount `<DomGuard />` monkey-patching `Node.prototype.removeChild` & `insertBefore`. 3) Add dynamic `key={`step-${step}`}` on wizard/tab containers so React cleanly replaces root containers. 4) Avoid split adjacent bare text nodes (`{a} · {b}`); use unified template literals (`${a} · ${b}`). |
| **Leaked foreign corporate branding and tracking SDKs** | Foreign prototypes often embed tracking pixels (Meta Pixel, CRM widgets), foreign LLC footers, and external GitHub/social links | Perform cleanroom sanitization: neutralize tracking widgets to `null`, scrub foreign social/repo URLs, update legal shells/footers to sovereign entity, and inject sovereign brand SVG emblem/favicon/manifest per `references/foreign_language_purge_and_ukrainian_adaptation.md`. |
| **Mention token regex breaks on localized tags** | Regex hardcoded to English/CJK tokens (e.g. `/@(?:card|photo|slide)\d+/i`) ignores Ukrainian tokens (`@картка`, `@фото`, `@слайд`), breaking autocomplete and pill highlights. | Broaden entity regex: `/@(?:card|картка|слайд|slide|photo|фото|p|к)\d+/iu`. |
| **Oversized placeholder breaks flex chat inputs** | Verbose localized placeholders (> 60-80 chars) wrap onto 3-4 lines in responsive sidebars or dock panels, displacing action buttons. | Enforce compact placeholders (≤ 50 chars), e.g. `"Запитайте про зміни (@ для вибору картки/фото)..."`. |
| **`TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'includes')` in payload sanitizers** | Stripping base64 images before LLM requests (`omitData`) blindly calls `.includes("data:")` on optional card/slide properties (`background`, `bg`) that are undefined or objects. | Guard with strict type checks: `typeof val === "string" && val.includes("data:")` before string operations. |
| **Residual CJK web fonts bloating bundle and misrendering Cyrillic** | Retaining fonts like `Pretendard`, `Noto Sans KR`, or `Nanum Myeongjo` adds unnecessary bundle overhead and produces inconsistent Cyrillic glyph heights. | Purge CJK fonts; standardize on `Inter` with `subsets: ['latin', 'cyrillic']` and Polaris Helix typography stacks. |
| **SSR / Next.js Hydration Crash: `localStorage.getItem is not a function`** | Evaluating `typeof localStorage !== "undefined"` or reading `localStorage` in initial component state initializers runs during Next.js Server-Side Rendering (Node.js/SSR environment where `localStorage` is undefined, mock object, or missing functions). | Always guard client storage in state initializers with `typeof window !== "undefined" && typeof localStorage !== "undefined" && localStorage?.getItem?.(...)` or move reads to a client-only `useEffect`. |
| **Rail / Global Navigation Language Toggle Desynchronization** | Mounting a language switcher only on the landing page while leaving deep studio routes (e.g. `/chat`, `/editor`) without a toggle isolates the user from switching languages. | Pin `LangToggle` into global persistent layout navigation (e.g. left `Rail` / navigation footer `rail-foot`), wrap route trees with `LangProvider`, and translate all tooltips, modal guides (`HelpGuide`), and studio wizard steps. |
| **`useLang` / `useTranslation` out of context on shared layouts or sub-routes** | Placing a localized component or toggle into a shared navigation bar (e.g. `<Rail />`) mounted across all routes, but only wrapping specific pages (like `/chat`) with `<LangProvider>`. Accessing other routes (like `/dashboard`, `/archive`) throws 500 runtime error: `useLang must be used inside <LangProvider>`. | Always hoist `<LangProvider>` to the root layout (`app/layout.tsx` or root `App.tsx`) wrapping `{children}` so every current and future route automatically inherits the i18n context. |
| **TypeScript Method Signature & Unused Style Drift during UI Translation** | Rewriting components with hypothetical API method names (e.g. `api.getGoals` vs `api.listGoals`) or leaving unused CSS objects (`const listStyle: React.CSSProperties = ...`) | Always inspect original service client types before refactoring form/data handlers; remove dangling style objects immediately to pass strict `tsc -b` and `noUnusedLocals` compiler flags. |

